ifies 100 L as the t = 0 level and 25 min from the start of filling."},{"n":57,"t":"assess_parts","p":"A linear sequence has u₅ = 34 and u₁₂ = 69. Find the common difference and the first term.\\n\\nb Find the general term uₙ, and use it to decide whether 250 is a term of this sequence.","d":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A linear sequence has u₅ = 34 and u₁₂ = 69. Find the common difference and the first term."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"b Find the general term uₙ, and use it to decide whether 250 is a term of this sequence."}]}]},"e":"Model answer — (a) Between u₅ and u₁₂ there are 7 steps: (69 − 34) ÷ 7 = 35 ÷ 7 = 5 = d. Then a₁ = 34 − 4 × 5 = 34 − 20 = 14. (b) uₙ = 14 + (n − 1) × 5 = 5n + 9. Is 250 a term? 5n + 9 = 250 → 5n = 241 → n = 48.2, which is not a whole number — 250 is NOT a term of the sequence (the nearest terms are u₄₈ = 249 and u₄₉ = 254).\\n\\nMarking — (a) 3 marks: 1 for d = 5 (method: (69 − 34) ÷ 7), 2 for a₁ = 14 (1 for setting up u₅ = a₁ + 4 × 5, 1 for 14). (b) 2 marks: 1 for uₙ = 5n + 9, 1 for solving the equation and concluding ‘not a term’ with the non-integer n = 48.2 shown. A bare ‘no’ without the equation scores 0 for the second mark.\\n\\nAcceptable alternates — ‘uₙ = 14 + 5(n−1)’ for the general term; conclusion phrased any way that shows the non-integer index.","m":5,"df":"hard","tp":"Linear Sequences","cfg":{"source":"myp5-full-formal-assessment-2026","question_number":57,"paper_section":"B","myp_criterion":"A","next_time_hint":"Seven steps between u₅ and u₁₂ — then test 250 in 5n + 9.","assessment_style":"formal_assessment","parts":[{"id":"a1","label":"(a) common difference","prompt":"Find the common difference.","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Between u₅ and u₁₂ there are 7 steps.","Divide the difference of the two known terms by the number of steps between them."],"answer":5,"tolerance":0},{"id":"a2","label":"(a) first term","prompt":"Find the first term.","kind":"numeric","points":2,"hints":["Rearrange u₅ = a₁ + 4d with your common difference and solve.","That gives the first term."],"answer":14,"tolerance":0},{"id":"b1","label":"(b) general term","prompt":"Find the general term uₙ.","kind":"expression","points":1,"hints":["Write the general term from the first term and the common difference.","Expand and simplify it."],"accepted":["uₙ = 5n + 9","un = 5n+9","5n+9","uₙ = 14 + 5(n − 1)","14 + 5(n-1)","u(n) = 5n + 9","5n + 9"]},{"id":"b2","label":"(b) is 250 a term?","prompt":"Decide whether 250 is a term of this sequence, showing your equation.","kind":"text","points":1,"hints":["Solve 5n + 9 = 250.","A term position must be a whole number — check yours against that requirement."],"accepted":["no — 5n + 9 = 250 gives n = 48.2, not a whole number, so 250 is not a term","250 is not a term; n = 241/5 = 48.2 is not an integer"],"keywords":[["no","not","isn’t","is not"],["48.2","241/5","48,2","not a whole","not an integer"]],"minKeywordGroups":2}],"marking":"Model answer — (a) Between u₅ and u₁₂ there are 7 steps: (69 − 34) ÷ 7 = 35 ÷ 7 = 5 = d. Then a₁ = 34 − 4 × 5 = 34 − 20 = 14. (b) uₙ = 14 + (n − 1) × 5 = 5n + 9. Is 250 a term? 5n + 9 = 250 → 5n = 241 → n = 48.2, which is not a whole number — 250 is NOT a term of the sequence (the nearest terms are u₄₈ = 249 and u₄₉ = 254).\\n\\nMarking — (a) 3 marks: 1 for d = 5 (method: (69 − 34) ÷ 7), 2 for a₁ = 14 (1 for setting up u₅ = a₁ + 4 × 5, 1 for 14). (b) 2 marks: 1 for uₙ = 5n + 9, 1 for solving the equation and concluding ‘not a term’ with the non-integer n = 48.2 shown. A bare ‘no’ without the equation scores 0 for the second mark.\\n\\nAcceptable alternates — ‘uₙ = 14 + 5(n−1)’ for the general term; conclusion phrased any way that shows the non-integer index.","marking_criteria":"Model answer — (a) Between u₅ and u₁₂ there are 7 steps: (69 − 34) ÷ 7 = 35 ÷ 7 = 5 = d. Then a₁ = 34 − 4 × 5 = 34 − 20 = 14. (b) uₙ = 14 + (n − 1) × 5 = 5n + 9. Is 250 a term? 5n + 9 = 